# Who owns what.
#
# GitHub's permissions are repo-wide — there is no per-folder write access — so
# this file does the next best thing: it makes the named owner an automatic,
# required reviewer for their paths. Nobody else changes these without them
# seeing it first.
#
# Ownership only takes effect for people with write access to this repository.

# Everything, unless a later line claims it.
*                                   @whiteoakmedia

# The Windows track. Validated on real Windows booth hardware, which the
# maintainer's own booth is not — @jpeters0 has the machine and owns these.
/WINDOWS.md                         @jpeters0
/scripts/build-windows.ps1          @jpeters0
/src-tauri/tauri.windows.conf.json  @jpeters0
/.github/workflows/windows.yml      @jpeters0

# Note: the Windows implementations inside shared files — the start-at-login
# and sleep-guard code in src-tauri/src/keepalive.rs, the NDI runtime lookup in
# ndi.rs, the OS facts and file-URL handling in diag.rs — cannot be owned by
# path, because they sit behind #[cfg(windows)] inside files that also carry
# the macOS paths. Changes there that touch a #[cfg(windows)] block should get
# @jpeters0 on the review regardless.
